<li>Zhao L, Huang F, Leun Hui A, Shen (2020). Bioactive Components and Health Benefits of Saskatoon Berry. J. of Diabetes Research. doi: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1155/2020/3901636">10.1155/2020/3901636</a></li>
<li>Michalczyk M, Macura R. (2010). Effect of Processing and Storage on the Antioxidant Activity of Frozen and Pasteurized Shadblow Serviceberry (Amelanchier Canadensis) [Internet]. [Accessed April 20 2025]. Int J. of Food Properties. 13:1225-1233. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/10942910903013407">https://doi.org/10.1080/10942910903013407</a></li>
<li>Zatylny M., Ziehl W.D., St-Pierre R.G. (2005) Physiochemical properties of fruit of 16 saskatoon (Amelanchier alnifolia Nutt.) cultivars [Internet]. Can J. Plant Sci. 85: 933-938. <a href="https://doi.org/10.4141/P04-065">https://doi.org/10.4141/P04-065</a></li>
<li><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">de Souza, D. R., Willems, J. L., &amp; Low, N. H. (2019). Phenolic composition and antioxidant activities of saskatoon berry fruit and pomace. </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Food Chemistry</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">290</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, 168–177. </span><a style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em" href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foodchem.2019.03.077">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foodchem.2019.03.077</a></li>
<li><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Fang, J. (2021). Nutritional composition of saskatoon berries: a review. </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Botany</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">99</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">(4), 175–184. </span><a style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em" href="https://doi.org/10.1139/cjb-2019-0191">https://doi.org/10.1139/cjb-2019-0191</a></li>
<li><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Juríková, T., Balla, S., Sochor, J., Pohanka, M., Mlcek, J., &amp; Baron, M. (2013). Flavonoid Profile of Saskatoon Berries (Amelanchier alnifolia Nutt.) and Their Health Promoting Effects. </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Molecules</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">18</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">(10), 12571–12586. </span><a style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em" href="https://doi.org/10.3390/molecules181012571">https://doi.org/10.3390/molecules181012571</a></li>
<li><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Ramachandran Vinayagam, &amp; Baojun Xu. (2015). Antidiabetic properties of dietary flavonoids: a cellular mechanism review. </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Nutrition &amp; Metabolism</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">12</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, 1–20. </span><a style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em" href="https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-015-0057-7">https://doi.org/10.1186/s12986-015-0057-7</a></li>
<li><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Splitrock Environmental. (n.d.). </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Saskatoon (tsáqwem). </em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Native Plants – Splitrock Environmental. </span><a style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em" href="https://splitrockenvironmental.ca/products/saskatoon-">https://splitrockenvironmental.ca/products/saskatoon-</a><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em"> tsaqwem?variant=40347094614182</span></li>
<li><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">Zatylny, A., Ziehl, W., &amp; St-Pierre, R. (2005). Physicochemical properties of fruit of 16 saskatoon (Amelanchier alnifolia Nutt.) cultivars. </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">CANADIAN JOURNAL OF PLANT SCIENCE</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">, </span><em style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">85</em><span style="text-align: initial;font-size: 1em">(4), 933–938.</span></li>
</ol>
</section>
